<title>POLAND: Polish broad money rises 2.3 pct in April - NBP.</title>
<headline>Polish broad money rises 2.3 pct in April - NBP.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-05-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Poland's broad money rose by 3.28 billion zlotys, or 2.3 percent, in April to 144.80 billion after a 2.2 pct rise in March, preliminary central bank figures showed on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Broad money grew 6.7 percent in the January-April period.  </p>
<p> BROAD POLISH MONEY		     APRIL     MARCH    APRIL 96</p>
<p>  month/month change (pct)	     2.3	 2.2	 2.7</p>
<p>  Money in bln zlotys		  144.80    141.51    113.64</p>
<p>  Foreign currency (in bln PLN)     25.36     25.00     21.36</p>
<p>  National currency		    119.44    116.51     92.28</p>
<p>  Cash in circulation		   25.86     24.59     21.96</p>
<p>  Lending to non-financial sector   90.29     87.83     60.87</p>
